# Follow Project Documents Exactly

Treat the project docs as the source of truth and implement behavior exactly as specified.

## Source Priority

1. Module docs under `docs/Layer 2 Modules/` for module-level contracts.
2. Foundation docs under `docs/Project Foundation/` for cross-cutting standards.
3. Architecture docs under `docs/PROJECT_ARCHITECTURE.md` and `docs/LAYER2_API_GATEWAY.md` for system constraints.

If documents conflict, call it out explicitly before coding and ask for resolution.

## Implementation Rules

- Do not invent or alter API paths, request/response shapes, status codes, auth rules, or error codes beyond the docs.
- Keep naming, route hierarchy, and middleware behavior aligned with documented contracts.
- Preserve documented non-functional constraints (security, logging, rate limiting, and audit expectations).
- When updating code, also update related artifacts (status report and Postman collection) to stay in sync with docs.

## Definition of Done

- Code behavior matches docs.
- Any deviations are documented and approved.
- Supporting artifacts remain consistent with the implemented/documented API surface.
